150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster-98x150.jpg 98w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster-195x300.jpg 195w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster-318x488.jpg 318w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster-768x1180.jpg 768w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster-59x90.jpg 59w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Im-All-Right-Jack-poster.jpg 1000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 98px) 100vw, 98px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"at-above-post-cat-page addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/celebrating-peter-sellers-im-all-right-jack-1959/\"></div><em>I’m All Right Jack</em> (1959), the Boulting Brothers satire on British industrial life in the 1950s, features one of Sellers's best remembered roles, as Fred Kite, the communist shop steward at the missile factory where Ian Carmichael's hapless Stanley Windrush has been sent to spy on the workers.<!-- AddThis Advanced Settings above via filter on get_the_excerpt --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings below via filter on get_the_excerpt --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings generic via filter on get_the_excerpt --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons above via filter on get_the_excerpt --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons below via filter on get_the_excerpt --><div class=\"at-below-post-cat-page addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/celebrating-peter-sellers-im-all-right-jack-1959/\"></div><!-- AddThis Share Buttons generic via filter on get_the_excerpt -->\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<h4 class=\"forwardLink\">[<a class=\"forwardLink\" hre