selected\"><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/events/\" >Events</a></li><li class=\"sf-drop-indicator\"><a style=\"cursor:default;\" href=\"javascript:void(0)\">The Collection</a><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/overview/\" >Overview</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/equipment/\" >Equipment</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/publications/\" >Publications</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/cinemas/\" >Cinemas</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/uniforms/\" >Uniforms</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/films/\" >Films</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/collection/advertising/\" >Advertising</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/shop/\" >Shop</a></li><li class=\"sf-drop-indicator\"><a style=\"cursor:default;\" href=\"javascript:void(0)\">About</a><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/about/history/\" >History</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/visit/\" >Visit Us</a></li><li><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/about/links/\" >Links</a></li></ul></li></ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"sf-blue-after\"></div>\r\n<!-- WP Menubar 5.9.3: end menu main_nav, template Suckerfish_41, CSS sf-blue.css -->\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                    @media screen and (-ms-high-contrast: active), (-ms-high-contrast: none) {\n                        /* Like IE9, which support conditional comments, IE10 needs less padding than the IE8 default */\n                        .sf-blue a, .sf-blue a:hover, .sf-blue a:visited { padding: 0 10.8px; }\n                    }\n                </style>\n\t\t<!--[if IE 9]>\n\t\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/plugins/menubar-templates/menubar-ie9.css\" media=\"screen\" />\n\t\t<![endif]-->\n\t\t<!--[if IE 7]>\n\t\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/plugins/menubar-templates/menubar-ie7.css\" media=\"screen\" />\n\t\t<![endif]-->\n\n\t</div>\r\n\t<div id=\"content_box\">\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t<div id=\"content\" class=\"posts\">\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\r\n<div class=\"navigation\">\r\n\t<span class=\"previous\">&larr; <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/the-gothique-film-society-presents-the-ghost-ship-1943-and-death-line-1972/\" rel=\"prev\">The Gothique Film Society presents <em>The Ghost Ship</em> (1943) and <em>Death Line</em> (1972)</a></span>\r\n\t<span class=\"next\"><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/screening-of-night-of-the-living-dead-1968-on-35mm-film/\" rel=\"next\">Screening of <em>Night of the Living Dead</em> (1968) on 35mm film</a> &rarr;</span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"clear whitespace\"></div>\r\n\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<div id=\"post-34245\" class=\"post-34245 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-events tag-contact tag-ticketlab\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"entry_header\">\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t\tRC: Comment and Edit functionality removed from following post header. Date reduced to Month and Year. Conditional 'Featured Article' added\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>The Gothique Film Society presents <em>Freaks</em> (1932) and <em>The Mask Of Fu Manchu</em> (1932)</h2>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h4>Fri 14 Mar 2025 @ 19:00 \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<!-- by David --> &middot; \r\n\t\t\t\t\t<!-- <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/the-gothique-film-society-presents-freaks-1932-and-the-mask-of-fu-manchu-1932/#comments\">No Comments</a> &middot; -->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/events/\" rel=\"category tag\">Events</a>\t\t\t\t\t<!--  -->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h4>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"entry\">\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t\tRC: I'm not clear when the_content pagination would be triggered.\r\n\t\t\t\t\tIf triggered, consider changing to plug-in based pagination.\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"at-above-post addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/the-gothique-film-society-presents-freaks-1932-and-the-mask-of-fu-manchu-1932/\"></div><p><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Freaks - click to enlarge\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-31965 size-large\" title=\"Freaks - click to enlarge\" src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2-488x381.jpg\" alt=\"Freaks\" width=\"488\" height=\"381\" srcset=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2-488x381.jpg 488w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2-300x234.jpg 300w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2-150x117.jpg 150w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2-90x70.jpg 90w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Freaks-2.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 488px) 100vw, 488px\" /></a>Founded in 1966, the Gothique Film Society specialises in double bills ‘for the connoisseur of the macabre’.</p>\n<p>We are delighted to be presenting two genuine classics from the Golden Age of Pre-Code* Horror!</p>\n<p><em>Freaks</em> opens our double bill of shockers produced by MGM in the wake of the massive artistic and financial successes of Universal’s <em>Dracula</em> and <em>Frankenstein</em>.</p>\n<p>The remit was to ‘outdo Universal’ – and, boy, did they succeed! (Even with cuts made for the US release, <em>Freaks</em> didn’t get a certificate in the UK until, unbelievably, 1963!)</p>\n<p>To cast the ‘freaks’, the studio scoured sideshows and carnivals. However, unlike their exploitation at those venues, the film treats them with the utmost respect: it is the ‘normal’ humans who are the ‘bad guys’, as beautiful trapeze artiste Cleopatra plots with her strongman lover to defraud dwarf Hans out of his fortune – with very unfortunate results in an unforgettable finale that remains as powerful today.</p>\n<p><em>The Mask of Fu Manchu</em> followed <em>Freaks</em> into production at MGM – and was substantially re-worked in the wake of the disastrous release of its predecessor. Even so, it’s still powerful stuff, with Boris Karloff at his hammiest as the title character, seeking the mask and sword of Genghis Khan in order to proclaim himself the reincarnation of the legendary conqueror and inflame the peoples of Asia and the Middle East into a war to wipe out the “white race”.</p>\n<p>His nemesis is British Secret Service agent Nayland Smith, who enlists prominent Egyptologist Sir Lionel Barton in his quest to beat Fu Manchu in the race for these fabulous treasures.</p>\n<p>In a fascinating sub-text, Sir Lionel’s daughter Sheila, who accompanies the expedition, comes to the attention of Fu Manchu’s daughter, a “sadistic nymphomaniac” who clearly has the hots for her!</p>\n<p>*”Pre-Code” refers to the period in the USA between the introduction of sound in 1929 and the rigid enforcement of the [censorship] Production Code in 1934. During this time the Code was routinely ignored, producing some of the most amazing – and outrageous &#8211; films.</p>\n<p>Doors open at 18.00 for a 19.00 start.</p>\n<p>Refreshments will be available in the licensed cafe/bar.</p>\n<h3>TICKETS &amp; PRICING</h3>\n<p>Everyone welcome: Individual tickets at £8.00 can be purchased on the door or via <a href=\"https://ticketlab.co.uk/event/id/27857#/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TicketLab</a>.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, Gothique Film Society membership subscriptions are available. Each season comprises six shows, from October to March. The subscription for all six shows is £30.00, but discounted membership is available for in-season joiners. For further enquiries about membership, contact David Simpson <a href=\"mailto:david.simpson399@btinternet.com\">david.simpson399@btinternet.com</a> or come along and join up on the door.<br />\n<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"The Mask of Fu Manchu - click to enlarge\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-34283 size-large\" title=\"The Mask of Fu Manchu - click to enlarge\" src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu-488x404.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"488\" height=\"404\" srcset=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu-488x404.jpg 488w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu-300x248.jpg 300w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu-150x124.jpg 150w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu-90x75.jpg 90w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/The-Mask-of-Fu-Manchu.jpg 628w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 488px) 100vw, 488px\" /></a></p>\n<!-- PHP 5.x --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings above via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings below via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings generic via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons above via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons below via filter on the_content --><div class=\"at-below-post addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/the-gothique-film-society-presents-freaks-1932-and-the-mask-of-fu-manchu-1932/\"></div><!-- AddThis Share Buttons generic via filter on the_content -->\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<script type='text/javascript'>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t//<![CDATA[\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdocument.write(\"<h4 class='backLink'>[<a href='javascript:history.back()' class='backLink' title='Go back'>&larr; Go back<\\/a>]<\\/h4>\");\r\n\t\t\t\t\t//]]>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</script>\t\t\t\t\t<noscript><h4 class='backLink'>[<a href=\"\" class='backLink' title='Go back'>&larr; Go back</a>]</h4></noscript>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t<p class=\"tagged\"><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/tag/contact/\" rel=\"tag\">Contact</a>&middot;<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/tag/ticketlab/\" rel=\"tag\">TicketLab</a></p>\t\t\t\tRC: Remove tag functionality and replace the 'clear' div with a flatter 'clear flat' one.\r\n-->\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"clear flat\"></div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\r\n<!--\t\t\r\n\t\t\tRC: Comment functionality removed. (IE8 fails to see this as comment, so commented the php also.)\r\n\t\t\t-->\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t<div id=\"sidebar\">\r\n\t<ul class=\"sidebar_list\">\r\n\t\t<li id=\"search-3\" class=\"widget widget_search\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Search</h2>\n<form method=\"get\" id=\"search_form\" action=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/\">\r\n\t<input type=\"text\" class=\"search_input\" value=\"To search, type and hit enter\" name=\"s\" id=\"s\" onfocus=\"if (this.value == 'To search, type and hit enter') {this.value = '';}\" onblur=\"if (this.value == '') {this.value = 'To search, type and hit enter';}\" />\r\n\t<input type=\"hidden\" id=\"searchsubmit\" value=\"Search\" />\r\n</form>\r\n</li>\n<li id=\"custom_html-5\" class=\"widget_text widget widget_custom_html\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Buy Advance Tickets From Ticketlab</h2>\n<div class=\"textwidget custom-html-widget\"><p class=\"final\"><a href=\"https://ticketlab.co.uk/events/CinemaMuseum\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img style=\"border:1px solid teal; height:200px\" \r\nsrc=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/ticketlab.png\" ></a></p></div></li>\n<li id=\"text-7\" class=\"widget widget_text\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Contact Us</h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"textwidget\"><p class=\"final\">The Cinema Museum<br /> \n2 Dugard Way (off Renfrew Road)<br />\nLondon SE11 4TH UK<br />\nTel.: 0207 840 2200<br />\nEmail: <a href=\"mailto:info@cinemamuseum.org.uk\">info@cinemamuseum.org.uk</a></p></div>\n\t\t</li>\n<li id=\"addthis_tool_by_class_name_widget-1\" class=\"widget widget_addthis_tool_by_class_name_widget\"><!-- Widget added by an AddThis plugin --><!-- widget name: AddThis Tool --><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Share this Page</h2>\n<div class=\"addthis_toolbox addthis_default_style \"><a class=\"addthis_button_facebook_like\" fb:like:layout=\"button_count\"></a><a class=\"addthis_button_tweet\"></a><a class=\"addthis_button_pinterest_pinit\"></a><a class=\"addthis_counter addthis_pill_style\"></a></div><!-- End of widget --></li>\n\t</ul>\r\n</div>\t\t\t\r\n\t</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"footer\">\n\t<div id=\"contact\">\n\t\t<p>The Cinema Museum\n\t\t\t<br />2 Dugard Way, London SE11 4TH\n\t\t\t<br />Tel.: +44 (0)20 7840 2200\n\t\t\t<br />Email:\n\t\t\t<a href=\"mailto:info@cinemamuseum.org.uk\">info@cinemamuseum.org.uk</a>\n\t\t</p>\n\t</div>\n\t<div id=\"copyright\">\n\t\t<p>&copy;\n\t\t\tThe Cinema Museum, London &mdash; Site by Antbird</p>\n\t</div>\n\t<div id=\"social_links\">\n\t\t<a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/pages/London/The-Cinema-Museum/94435861815\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/facebook.jpg\" alt=\"Visit The Cinema Museum on Facebook\" title=\"Visit The Cinema Museum on Facebook\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"http://twitter.com/CinemaMuseum\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/twitter.png\" alt=\"Follow The Cinema Museum on Twitter\" title=\"Follow The Cinema Museum on Twitter\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a>\n\t\t<!-- Removed obso