et\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/plugins/menubar-templates/menubar-ie9.css\" media=\"screen\" />\n\t\t<![endif]-->\n\t\t<!--[if IE 7]>\n\t\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/plugins/menubar-templates/menubar-ie7.css\" media=\"screen\" />\n\t\t<![endif]-->\n\n\t</div>\r\n\t<div id=\"content_box\">\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t<div id=\"content\" class=\"posts\">\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\r\n<div class=\"navigation\">\r\n\t<span class=\"previous\">&larr; <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/special-bollywood-fundraiser-for-the-cinema-museum/\" rel=\"prev\">Special Bollywood fundraiser for The Cinema Museum</a></span>\r\n\t<span class=\"next\"><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/exploding-cinema-september/\" rel=\"next\">Exploding Cinema September</a> &rarr;</span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"clear whitespace\"></div>\r\n\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<div id=\"post-33715\" class=\"post-33715 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-events tag-contact tag-ticketlab\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"entry_header\">\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t\tRC: Comment and Edit functionality removed from following post header. Date reduced to Month and Year. Conditional 'Featured Article' added\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Misty Moon Presents George Layton Tells Fibs and Stories</h2>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h4>Sat 31 May 2025 @ 19:00 \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<!-- by David --> &middot; \r\n\t\t\t\t\t<!-- <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/misty-moon-presents-george-layton-tells-fibs-and-stories/#comments\">No Comments</a> &middot; -->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/topics/events/\" rel=\"category tag\">Events</a>\t\t\t\t\t<!--  -->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</h4>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"entry\">\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t\tRC: I'm not clear when the_content pagination would be triggered.\r\n\t\t\t\t\tIf triggered, consider changing to plug-in based pagination.\r\n-->\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"at-above-post addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/misty-moon-presents-george-layton-tells-fibs-and-stories/\"></div><p><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"George Layton - click to enlarge\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-33716 size-large\" title=\"George Layton - click to enlarge\" src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton-390x488.png\" alt=\"George Layton\" width=\"390\" height=\"488\" srcset=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton-390x488.png 390w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton-240x300.png 240w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton-120x150.png 120w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton-72x90.png 72w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/George-Layton.png 480w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 390px) 100vw, 390px\" /></a>George Layton is probably best known as a theatre, film and TV actor: The <em>Doctor in the House</em>/ <em>Doctor In Charge</em>/ <em>DoctorAt Large</em> series (1969-91); <em>It Ain’t Half Hot, Mum</em> (1974-75); <em>Minder </em>(1979-82); <em>The Sweeney</em> (1975); <em>EastEnders</em> (2011-12); Fagin in <em>Oliver!</em>; Mr Cellophane in <em>Chicago</em>. In the early 1970s he started the long-running Sunday night BBC TV <em>“That’s Life”</em> with Esther Rantzen.</p>\n<p>He has also had a successful writing career, having created two award-winning television series<em> Don’t Wait Up</em> (six series, 1984-90) starring Nigel Havers and the recently late Tony Britton, and <em>Executive Stress</em> (three series, 1986-88) starring Penelope Keith.</p>\n<p>George also wrote many of the various <em>“Doctor”</em> series, as well as <em>My Brother’s Keeper</em> (1975-76), <em>Robin’s Nest</em> (1979-81), and early shows for <em>On The Buses</em> (1972-73).</p>\n<p>However, Misty Moon supporters may not be aware of his best-selling books, <em>The Fib</em>, <em>The Swap</em> and <em>The Trick</em>, three celebrated collections of linked short stories focusing on post-war Britain, each story narrated by a nameless self-confessed coward from a single parent family.</p>\n<p>Tonight, George will talk about balancing what was an already successful acting career with what became a full time writing career, and will read some of his stories evoking memories of the 1950s.</p>\n<p>After the show there will be a meet and greet with the audience and chance to purchase George’s books.</p>\n<p><em><strong><a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"The Fib book cover - click to enlarge\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-33717 size-medium\" title=\"The Fib book cover - click to enlarge\" src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover-198x300.jpg\" alt=\"The Fib book cover\" width=\"198\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover-198x300.jpg 198w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover-323x488.jpg 323w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover-99x150.jpg 99w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover-60x90.jpg 60w, http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/The-Fib-cover.jpg 330w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\" /></a>The Fib And Other Stories</strong></em><strong>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>‘Funny and moving…a rare gift’ (<em>The Guardian</em>)</li>\n<li>‘Angst, cringing embarrassment and, above all, humour ensure that this still has readers in stitches today.’ (<em>TES</em>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em><strong>The Swap And Other Stories</strong></em><strong>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>‘Well worth waiting for… written in the rueful school of childhood hard knocks perfected by Bill Naughton, with whom Layton can stand comparison…’ (<em>The Independent</em>)</li>\n<li>‘…evocative stories, tough, funny and tender by turns… a nostalgic whiff of the fifties…’ (<em>The Guardian</em>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em><strong>The Trick And Other Stories</strong></em><strong>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>‘…immensely gratifying to find Layton’s world just as compelling as ever… The stories unerringly conjure up the atmosphere of war-weary early 1950s England, each is superbly crafted…’ (<em>School Librarian</em>)</li>\n<li>‘George Layton is a rare writer. He has a compelling way of telling tales – unputdownable’ (Michael Morpurgo)</li>\n<li>‘…robust storylines and shrewd humour, though Layton deals with some edgier themes, and deftly plays with timelines to enhance suspense’ (<em>Books for Keeps</em>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Doors open at 18.00, for a 19.00 start.</p>\n<p>Refreshments will be available in our licensed cafe/bar.</p>\n<h3>TICKETS &amp; PRICING</h3>\n<p>Tickets £20.<br />\nAdvance tickets may be purchased from <a href=\"https://ticketlab.co.uk/event/id/28168\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ticketlab</a>, or direct from the Museum by calling 020 7840 2200 in office hours.</p>\n<!-- PHP 5.x --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings above via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings below via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Advanced Settings generic via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons above via filter on the_content --><!-- AddThis Share Buttons below via filter on the_content --><div class=\"at-below-post addthis_tool\" data-url=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/2024/misty-moon-presents-george-layton-tells-fibs-and-stories/\"></div><!-- AddThis Share Buttons generic via filter on the_content -->\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<script type='text/javascript'>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t//<![CDATA[\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdocument.write(\"<h4 class='backLink'>[<a href='javascript:history.back()' class='backLink' title='Go back'>&larr; Go back<\\/a>]<\\/h4>\");\r\n\t\t\t\t\t//]]>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</script>\t\t\t\t\t<noscript><h4 class='backLink'>[<a href=\"\" class='backLink' title='Go back'>&larr; Go back</a>]</h4></noscript>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n<!--\r\n\t\t\t\t<p class=\"tagged\"><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/tag/contact/\" rel=\"tag\">Contact</a>&middot;<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/tag/ticketlab/\" rel=\"tag\">TicketLab</a></p>\t\t\t\tRC: Remove tag functionality and replace the 'clear' div with a flatter 'clear flat' one.\r\n-->\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"clear flat\"></div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\r\n<!--\t\t\r\n\t\t\tRC: Comment functionality removed. (IE8 fails to see this as comment, so commented the php also.)\r\n\t\t\t-->\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t<div id=\"sidebar\">\r\n\t<ul class=\"sidebar_list\">\r\n\t\t<li id=\"search-3\" class=\"widget widget_search\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Search</h2>\n<form method=\"get\" id=\"search_form\" action=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/\">\r\n\t<input type=\"text\" class=\"search_input\" value=\"To search, type and hit enter\" name=\"s\" id=\"s\" onfocus=\"if (this.value == 'To search, type and hit enter') {this.value = '';}\" onblur=\"if (this.value == '') {this.value = 'To search, type and hit enter';}\" />\r\n\t<input type=\"hidden\" id=\"searchsubmit\" value=\"Search\" />\r\n</form>\r\n</li>\n<li id=\"custom_html-5\" class=\"widget_text widget widget_custom_html\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Buy Advance Tickets From Ticketlab</h2>\n<div class=\"textwidget custom-html-widget\"><p class=\"final\"><a href=\"https://ticketlab.co.uk/events/CinemaMuseum\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img style=\"border:1px solid teal; height:200px\" \r\nsrc=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/ticketlab.png\" ></a></p></div></li>\n<li id=\"text-7\" class=\"widget widget_text\"><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Contact Us</h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"textwidget\"><p class=\"final\">The Cinema Museum<br /> \n2 Dugard Way (off Renfrew Road)<br />\nLondon SE11 4TH UK<br />\nTel.: 0207 840 2200<br />\nEmail: <a href=\"mailto:info@cinemamuseum.org.uk\">info@cinemamuseum.org.uk</a></p></div>\n\t\t</li>\n<li id=\"addthis_tool_by_class_name_widget-1\" class=\"widget widget_addthis_tool_by_class_name_widget\"><!-- Widget added by an AddThis plugin --><!-- widget name: AddThis Tool --><h2 class=\"widgettitle\">Share this Page</h2>\n<div class=\"addthis_toolbox addthis_default_style \"><a class=\"addthis_button_facebook_like\" fb:like:layout=\"button_count\"></a><a class=\"addthis_button_tweet\"></a><a class=\"addthis_button_pinterest_pinit\"></a><a class=\"addthis_counter addthis_pill_style\"></a></div><!-- End of widget --></li>\n\t</ul>\r\n</div>\t\t\t\r\n\t</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"footer\">\n\t<div id=\"contact\">\n\t\t<p>The Cinema Museum\n\t\t\t<br />2 Dugard Way, London SE11 4TH\n\t\t\t<br />Tel.: +44 (0)20 7840 2200\n\t\t\t<br />Email:\n\t\t\t<a href=\"mailto:info@cinemamuseum.org.uk\">info@cinemamuseum.org.uk</a>\n\t\t</p>\n\t</div>\n\t<div id=\"copyright\">\n\t\t<p>&copy;\n\t\t\tThe Cinema Museum, London &mdash; Site by Antbird</p>\n\t</div>\n\t<div id=\"social_links\">\n\t\t<a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/pages/London/The-Cinema-Museum/94435861815\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/facebook.jpg\" alt=\"Visit The Cinema Museum on Facebook\" title=\"Visit The Cinema Museum on Facebook\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"http://twitter.com/CinemaMuseum\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/twitter.png\" alt=\"Follow The Cinema Museum on Twitter\" title=\"Follow The Cinema Museum on Twitter\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a>\n\t\t<!-- Removed obsolete items ... PC 2/2/18\n\t\t<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/user/CinemaMuseum\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/youtube-logo.gif\" alt=\"Visit The Cinema Museum's YouTube Channel\" title=\"Visit The Cinema Museum's YouTube Channel\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a> \n\t\t<a href=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/feed/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Syndicate this site using RSS\">\n\t\t\t<img src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/themes/Cutline-1-1.4-2ColumnRight/images/rss.png\" alt=\"Subscribe to the Cinema Museum's RSS Feed\" title=\"Subscribe to the Cinema Museum's RSS Feed\"\n\t\t\t/>\n\t\t</a>-->\n\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"full_clear very_flat\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!--Powered by eShop v6.3.14 by Rich Pedley http://www.quirm.net/--><!-- Lightbox Plus v2.0.5 - 2010.07.02 - Message: 0-->\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\njQuery(document).ready(function($){\n  $(\"a[rel*=lightbox]\").colorbox({opacity:0.8});\n});\n</script>\n<script>\r\n  (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i['GoogleAnalyticsObject']=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){\r\n  (i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o),\r\n  m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m)\r\n  })(window,document,'script','//www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js','ga');\r\n\r\n  ga('create', 'UA-41628024-1', 'cinemamuseum.org.uk');\r\n  ga('send', 'pageview');\r\n\r\n</script>\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"http://www.cinemamuseum.org.uk/wordpress/wp-content/plugins/lightbox-plus/js/jquery.colorbox-min.js?ver=1.3.8\" id=\"lightbox-js\"></script>\n</body>\n\n</html>"
